Replaced the four separate member initializations with a single `memcpy` of the contiguous derived-member block, letting the compiler emit wider loads/stores while preserving the base class copy.

```cpp
#include <cstring>

Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
{
    std::memcpy(&profile, &field.profile,
                reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&field.isFieldExpanded) + sizeof(field.isFieldExpanded)
                - reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&field.profile));
}
```